<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept beef imports plunge 38.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept beef imports plunge 38.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in September were 34,542 tonnes, down 38.3 percent from the same period a year earlier, according to data released by the Finance Ministry on Tuesday. Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Sept 96     Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p> Total	    34,542	42,444	56,010</p>
<p> Refrigerated   20,530	25,938	31,043</p>
<p> Frozen	   14,012	16,506	24,967</p>
<p> Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     11,437	15,003	18,819</p>
<p>  U.S.	     8,533	 9,965	11,423</p>
<p> Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Sept 96     Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p> U.S.		8,048	28,727	15,947</p>
<p> Australia	 4,757	15,632	 7,348</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first nine months of 1996 were 240,582 tonnes against 267,376 tonnes during the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the first nine months of 1996 came to 253,512 tonnes against 212,156 tonnes in the same period of 1995. -- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
